When blessed and enchanted, arrows rarely disappear.

All I know is that 50 poisoned +6 arrows will last you
from the beginning of the sanctum (those high priests
are not poison resistant) all the way to the planes.

Then you'll need more than 50 arrows for Astral, not
because you lose them, but because there are too many
targets, and you don't have time to pick them up. :-)

Poison is great however, and I'll take the chance for
instant-killing high-priests over the strength bonus,
especially if I was elvish.

Daggers however, are a great backup weapon; even a
great main weapon till you get the stack of arrows
you need from the bow.

Course, the best of the best are darts, which give
you the bonuses of the dagger, with the bonuses
of the arrows. You can poison them, they weigh
10x lighter than daggers, and rarely disappear
when enchanted.

I still prefer weilding the Longbow however, so
Arrows it is for me. I usually don't collect darts
throughout the dungeon.

